/**
 * Recipe — cart-line inline status message (SFCC-795 §11.2, plan step 3.2).
 * `.claude/session-notes.md` §11.2: "inline message (error/warning) sits between the stepper and
 * the actions, w-full, `Default/Caption` regular 12px / lh18. In error states the Item Details
 * gap widens 12 -> 16px." (the gap widening is `ZimmCartItem`'s own `hasError` resolution prop —
 * see product-item.css.ts — not this recipe's concern; this file owns only the message's own
 * type/colour/icon.)
 *
 * Two-part multipart recipe (`root`/`text`), following zimmDrawer.css.ts's plain-object
 * `{parts, baseStyle, variants}` shape rather than `defineStyleConfig` — no Chakra helper
 * factory, same Chakra-native string `variants` resolution either form supports.
 *
 * Restructured from a single-node `defineStyleConfig` (SFCC-795 rework — Marcel's own visual
 * checkpoint against the real Figma file surfaced a genuine gap the original single-node shape
 * couldn't express): the `warning` variant carries a leading 16x16 icon, the `error` variant
 * never does. This was already a known requirement, not something discovered fresh at the
 * checkpoint or borrowed from an unrelated ticket — `.claude/session-notes.md:395` (the original
 * SFCC-795 ticket restatement, written before any Figma metadata was pulled) already says
 * "warning state (grey info icon + message, e.g. 'Maximum purchase quantity reached for this
 * size')", the exact copy string used here. It was simply dropped somewhere between that
 * restatement and the written build plan's step 3.2 text, and the checkpoint is what caught it.
 *
 * Confirmed against 3 real cart-item instances in Figma file QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs
 * ("Zimmermann_Designs") — the two error-copy states (FULLY OOS node 9323-101979, PARTIAL OOS
 * node 9323-98397) have a bare `<text>` message sub-tree, no icon; the warning-copy state's own
 * "Cart Item" instance is `icon(16x16, x=0) -> 8px gap -> text(x=24)`. That instance is node
 * 9323:106685, named "Cart Item" — confirmed via its own metadata to be one of 5 per-item rows
 * inside the "Cart-item-group" frame, i.e. genuinely SFCC-270/795's own per-item scope. It is
 * NOT the same as "Cart-level-messages" (a distinct sibling instance, 1186x52, that the same
 * top-level "WARNINGS SHOWN" frame (9323-90299) also contains at the page level) — that one is
 * SFCC-404's cart-level banner, a wholly different component this build does not touch. The two
 * share a parent frame and a similar 8px gap value, which is what makes them easy to conflate at
 * a glance; the "Cart Item"/"Cart-level-messages" instance names are what actually disambiguate
 * them, confirmed directly rather than inferred from proximity.
 *
 * So the single implicit node this recipe used to describe is no longer enough: `root` is now
 * the flex row wrapping the optional icon + the text, and `text` carries what used to be the
 * whole recipe's `baseStyle`.
 *
 * No separate `icon` part: `ZimmIcon`'s own `color` prop defaults to `currentColor`
 * (zimmIcon/index.tsx), and Chakra's `Icon` component passes `color` straight through as the
 * rendered SVG's own inline CSS `color` rather than resolving it to a token itself (confirmed
 * directly in `@chakra-ui/icon`'s `Icon` implementation) — so the icon element's own
 * `stroke="currentColor"` shapes (zimm.tsx's `InfoSolidIcon`) inherit `root`'s `color` via
 * ordinary CSS inheritance for free. Nothing to declare on this recipe's side for the icon.
 *
 * --- Typography: regular weight is a DELIBERATE override, on a DIFFERENT Figma node than the
 * one commit 5 (SFCC-270) corrected — read both before touching either ---
 * `textStyle: 'caption'` supplies the correct 12px size / 18px line-height pair, but this
 * codebase's `caption` textStyle (theme/foundation/typography.ts) is MEDIUM-weight
 * (`fontWeight: fontWeights.medium`) — that is exactly right for Figma's OTHER caption node,
 * `Default/Caption-strong` (the cart-item colour+size line — see
 * item-variant/item-variant.css.ts:73-84, which deliberately keeps `caption` with NO fontWeight
 * override for that reason, having removed an earlier, backwards override). THIS element is
 * Figma's plain, un-strong `Default/Caption` node, which is REGULAR-weight per the session-notes
 * citation above — the opposite correction, on a different string, elsewhere in the same design
 * file. `fontWeight` is therefore set explicitly below, on the `text` part, to override the
 * textStyle-expanded medium value back down to regular — the same "a direct CSS prop applied
 * after the textStyle expansion wins in Chakra's style pipeline" mechanism zimmButton.css.ts's
 * `sizes.lg`/`sizes.sm` already documents and relies on for the identical reason.
 *
 * `root.width: 'full'` reproduces Figma's own "w-full" annotation for this element explicitly,
 * rather than relying on this node's flex/stack parent to stretch it by default — moved here
 * from the (no-longer-existing) single node, since `root` is now the outer container.
 *
 * `root.alignItems: 'flex-start'`: top-aligned, not centred — the warning icon sits at the top
 * of what can be 2-line-wrapped text, not vertically centred against it. Confirmed via the
 * Figma metadata's own y-positions on the "Cart Item" instance cited above (9323:106685): the
 * icon instance sits at y=0 within its frame, the same top edge the text frame starts from.
 *
 * `root.gap: 'var(--zimm-scale-xs)'` (8px): that same "Cart Item" instance places the 16px-wide icon at
 * x=0 and the text frame starting at x=24 — the 8px difference between them is the gap.
 *
 * Three variants, not two — corrected SFCC-795 plan step 3.3, 2026-09-18 (Marcel's direct Figma
 * inspector pull for the discount-label node). This paragraph used to read "the variants map
 * below only ever has the two keys `error`/`warning`; do not add a third," citing "SFCC-795
 * §11.2 build decisions" for that count. That citation does not hold up under a direct check:
 * `.claude/session-notes.md`'s actual "## 11.2 Cart Item" section (lines 710-740) never mentions
 * low-stock at all — checked directly, not assumed. The real, verifiable source for "no
 * low-stock messaging in the cart" is `.docs/prd/cart.md:70` (CAI-030): "Low-stock indicator
 * shown at size level — no quantity number displayed; not displayed in mini-cart or cart." That
 * prohibition is real and unchanged by this correction — a `LOW` size-level stock indicator has
 * no business rendering on a cart line regardless of how many variants this recipe has. What was
 * wrong was the COUNT, not the prohibition: `error`/`success`/`warning` are three real,
 * Figma-sourced cart-item-level treatments (this file's own docblock above cites each); a
 * fourth, low-stock-specific key is what remains forbidden.
 */
const baseStyle = {
  root: {
    display: 'flex',
    alignItems: 'flex-start',
    gap: 'var(--zimm-scale-xs)',
    width: 'full',
  },
  text: {
    textStyle: 'caption',
    fontWeight: 'var(--zimm-font-weight-regular)',
    // Standard flexbox text-truncation-prevention: without these, a long message next to the
    // fixed-size icon in this flex row can be squeezed narrower than its own content instead of
    // wrapping onto its own available width. `flex: 1` lets the text claim the row's remaining
    // space (the icon, an intrinsically-sized SVG, takes only what it needs); `minWidth: 0`
    // overrides a flex item's own default `min-width: auto`, which would otherwise refuse to
    // shrink the text below its content's intrinsic width and push `root` wider than its own
    // `width: full`.
    flex: 1,
    minWidth: 0,
  },
};

const variants = {
  // Figma `text/error` #9c0000 -> status.error (session-notes.md §11.10(6) colour audit).
  error: {
    root: {
      color: 'var(--zimm-color-status-error)',
    },
  },
  // Figma "Default/Caption" success text (cart-line discount label, "20% off applied") — pulled
  // directly by Marcel via Figma inspector, 2026-09-18: `color: var(--alias-color-text-success,
  // #2D5A3D)`. Byte-identical to this codebase's own status.success token: green[500] =
  // '#2d5a3d' (theme/foundation/colour.ts:27,80), registered as var(--zimm-color-status-success)
  // in zimmTokens.ts:73 — not a new token, the existing one. No icon on this variant, confirmed
  // directly with Marcel — same no-icon behaviour as `error` (see index.tsx's icon condition,
  // unchanged by this addition).
  success: {
    root: {
      color: 'var(--zimm-color-status-success)',
    },
  },
  // Figma `text/muted` / `text/subtlest` #969696 -> both collapse onto this one token, no
  // ambiguity in this codebase's own set (session-notes.md §11.10(6)). This is also the same
  // token the InfoSolidIcon's own real Figma export colour (#969696) coincidentally matches —
  // see that icon's own citation in zimm.tsx — not a second, independent confirmation of the
  // token choice, just a coincidence worth noting there and here.
  //
  // Max-quantity messaging ("Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size") uses THIS variant,
  // not `error` — even though its own requirement/AC text uses the word "error" to describe it.
  // That word is describing "user-facing feedback" in the requirement's own vocabulary, not
  // asserting the error SEVERITY tier: the actual Figma design and that story's own AC agree the
  // rendered treatment is grey/warning, not red/error. Deliberate word-vs-severity reconciliation,
  // settled at this build's planning gate — not a mistake, and not to be "corrected" back to
  // `error` by a future reader matching the word alone.
  warning: {
    root: {
      color: 'var(--zimm-color-text-muted)',
    },
  },
};

export const ZimmInlineMessage = {
  parts: ['root', 'text'],
  baseStyle,
  variants,
};

